0..52 Comment "//! This fixture writes a `match` in a type\'s place."
53..56 Comment "//!"
57..135 Comment "//! The checker expands a call in a type, and the printer then writes the code"
136..212 Comment "//! of the decode as a `match`. So the reader takes that `match` back, as it"
213..230 Comment "//! takes a call."
231..234 Comment "//!"
235..310 Comment "//! The type is the decode of the code that the match returns. A match on a"
311..390 Comment "//! constructor reduces to the type that its arm returns. A match on a variable"
391..468 Comment "//! stays stuck, and its decode stays with it. Each arm returns its code with"
469..536 Comment "//! `pure`. A `return` needs a body, and a type\'s place is no body."
537..540 Comment "//!"
541..557 Comment "//! - see: #7564"
